@title Course completion, Fall 2024 to Spring 2026
@subtitle Online and blended courses, for the academic senate on 2026-11-10
@author Dr. Aaliyah Brandt, Institutional Research

## Completion at a glance
kpi Completion rate | 79.0% | +9 pts since Fall 2024 | good
kpi Students completed | 1,187 | Spring 2026 | good
kpi Online completion | 68.1% | 18 pts below in-person | bad

Completion rose from 70.0% in Fall 2024 to 79.0% in Spring 2026, a gain of 9 points in four terms. The biggest single jump, 5 points, came in Fall 2025, when free tutoring for first-year students started on 2025-08-25.

## Term by term
data terms = term,enrolled,completed,completion rate; Fall 2024,1240,868,70.0; Spring 2025,1315,947,72.0; Fall 2025,1410,1086,77.0; Spring 2026,1502,1187,79.0

chart line terms y=completion rate unit=% labels title="Completion rate by term"

table terms

## By format, Spring 2026
data fmt = format,enrolled,completed,completion rate; In person,520,447,86.0; Hybrid,600,480,80.0; Online,382,260,68.1

chart hbar fmt y=completion rate unit=% labels target="79 overall" title="Completion rate by delivery format, Spring 2026"

Online courses complete at 68.1%, about 18 points below in-person courses at 86.0%. Online is the format with the most room to improve.

## Notes
- Completed means a passing grade. It does not measure attendance.
- Withdrawals before the census date, on the 15th day of the term, are not counted as enrolled.
